  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified OAI 697 days before the posting",
  "headline_cites": ["E23", "E19", "D11"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA lists sodium bicarbonate injection as a current shortage first posted 2017-03-01 and still current as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["E50", "D11"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Multiple manufacturers are on the shortage list including Exela Pharma Sciences, LLC, Hospira, Inc., Amphastar Pharmaceuticals, Inc., Fresenius Kabi USA, LLC, and Long Grove Pharmaceuticals LLC.",
      "cites": ["E45", "E46", "E47", "E48", "E49"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Our Corvale General supply of 84 mg/mL 50 mL vials (NDC 51754500105) is labeled by Exela Pharma Sciences, LLC.",
      "cites": ["E4"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Exela Pharma Sciences, LLC (FEI 3008563008) received an OAI classification on 2024-11-15, which was 697 days before the 2026-10-21 check date.",
      "cites": ["E23", "E19", "D11"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The same plant also received a Warning Letter on 2025-07-02.",
      "cites": ["E21", "E22"]
    },
    {
      "text": "An alternate manufacturer A-S Medication Solutions (NDC 50090681300) is available at Corvale General and approved for interchange by P&T on 2025-12-08.",
      "cites": ["E5", "E52"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The highest-ranked action is to transfer 211 vials of 84 mg/mL 50 mL from Corvale General to Corvale East, which would raise Corvale East from 6.1 to 14 days on hand while Corvale General retains 22 days.",
      "cites": ["D12", "D1", "D2"]
    }
  ]
}
